 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-71",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints the number (5.71) on an empty line under (5.70); no equation is missing."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-k-i",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints $\\knu_i\\kchi_i/2c = \\knref_i\\knu_i/c$. With $\\knref_i = 1 + \\kchi_i/2$, $\\knu_i\\kchi_i/2c = (\\knref_i - 1)\\knu_i/c$, the medium's addition to the wavevector $\\kkmag_i = \\knref_i\\knu_i/c$. The difference $\\kDeltakmis = \\kkmag_1 + \\kkmag_2 - \\kkmag_3$ holds all the same, because the vacuum parts $\\knu_i/c$ cancel when $\\knu_3 = \\knu_1 + \\knu_2$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-delta-k",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints $\\kDeltakmis \\approx \\frac{\\knu_3}{c}(\\knref_3 - 1) \\approx 2\\frac{\\knu_3}{c}\\kchi_3^{(1)}$. With $\\knref_3 - 1 = \\kchi_3^{(1)}/2$ and $\\kchi_3$ dominant, Eq. (5.75) gives $\\kDeltakmis \\approx -\\frac{\\knu_3}{c}(\\knref_3 - 1) = -\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\knu_3}{c}\\kchi_3^{(1)}$."
  }
 ],
